                <pb facs="0392" n="280" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg280"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/4193b: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Commission to
                        Negotiate Peace</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-03-31T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 31, 1919,
                                5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1393. Referring Department’s telegram March 29 concerning repatriation
                    Czecho-Slovak forces in Siberia, the Secretary of War asks me to say that he
                    feels some definite action is extremely important.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
